      "content": "The E15 error code on your Bosch dishwasher is a common issue, but it's a bit of a tricky one to diagnose. You're on the right track by checking the leak sensor, but I'm afraid it's not as simple as just finding the leak sensor and drying it off. You'll need to follow a more methodical approach, like a resourceful little house-elf navigating a complex network of pipes and ducts.\n\nFirst, make sure you've checked the manual and the Bosch website for any specific troubleshooting guides for your model. If that doesn't help, you can try resetting the dishwasher by pressing the \"Reset\" button (usually located at the bottom of the control panel) and then letting it run a cycle. This might clear any temporary errors and allow you to diagnose the issue further.\n\nTo check the leak sensor, you'll need to locate it, which can be a bit of a challenge, especially if you're not familiar with the dishwasher's internal workings. The leak sensor is usually located near the bottom of the dishwasher, and it might be a small, round or oval-shaped component with a wire connected to it. You can try using a multimeter to test the sensor's electrical connections, but be careful not to damage",
